 offers pants, shorts, tops, and jackets for athletic activities, such as yoga, running, training, and other activities. The company also provides fitness-inspired accessories. It sells its products through company-operated stores; seasonal stores, pop-ups, university campus retailers, and yoga and fitness studios; outlets; Like New, a re-commerce program; and its e-commerce website. The company was founded in 1998 and is based in Vancouver, Canada.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Heidi L. O'Neill | CEO & Director | Age 60","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 39K people. Revenue per employee of $285K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 20%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $24K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10). Active legal proceedings include employment or labour-related filings.","financial_summary":["lululemon athletica inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $12.8B market cap on $11.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +18% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 37% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 27-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 56% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $922M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.01\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Management returns a meaningful 9.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.6% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 10% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 25% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 50% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.9M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Gross margin tops the Consumer Cyclical peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"SHAREHOLDER ALERT: Bronstein Gewirtz & Grossman, LLC Announces Class Action Against Lululemon Athletica Inc. (NASDAQ: LULU) -- Investors Who Suffered Losses Are Encouraged to Contact the Firm","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/shareholder-alert-bronstein-gewirtz--grossman-llc-announces-class-action-against-lululemon-athletica-inc-nasdaq-lulu--investors-who-suffered-losses-are-encouraged-to-contact-the-firm-302928104.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793984400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.756,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"Shai Gilgeous-Alexander to cut ribbon at OKC\u2019s new La La Land Cafe\u2019s grand opening","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/shai-gilgeous-alexander-cut-ribbon-215526000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794004165.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.9,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Lululemon names brand, strategy chiefs in latest executive shakeup","source":"bnnbloomberg.ca","link":"https://www.bnnbloomberg.ca/business/company-news/2026/11/06/lululemon-names-brand-strategy-chiefs-in-latest-executive-shakeup/","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794001888.183,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.153,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"lululemon Appoints Ben Hallam as Chief Brand Officer to Strengthen Global Brand and Guest Experience","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/small-business/articles/lululemon-appoints-ben-hallam-chief-210500187.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793999100.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.765,"tier":2,"scope