 0.0x net debt to EBITDA ($1.4B of cash against $2.1B of debt), with interest covered 2150.4x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 5.5, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.26)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 11.0% over 3 years, 20.3% over 5 years and 18.3% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 27% of profits supports about 9.9% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 9.9% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 58%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.4x, 6.1% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 28, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 4.6%, and institutions hold 80%.","Insider trading is two-way: 2 purchases and 1 sale over the past year, net $895K bought.","It returns 9.2% a year to shareholders (9.2% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 3.0% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 15.4% of the float, 3.4 days to cover."],"people":["With about 39,000 employees, each generates about $285K of revenue, 0.7x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 20.1% a year.","That works out to $24K of free cash flow per employee.","Compensation governance scores poorly (10/10, lower is better).","Culture flags: employment-related legal filings.","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":83,"head":"Invest: trades 25% below fair value of $148; ROIC 36.8% vs WACC 10.2%.","pros":["Model rating BUY (composite 73, gates 21/25)","Trades 25% below fair value of $148","ROIC 36.8% vs WACC 10.2%","Revenue grew 20.3%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.0x"],"cons":["28 analysts' mean target $104 (-6%)","12-1 month momentum -43%"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":125.95,"vc":{"base":148.17,"base_src":"dcf","bear":110.85,"bull":202.73,"alt_median":210.45,"n